From f953653654de5adc88e31ecb529440eef130836e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cvp1 <54213066+cvp1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:08:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GFSK8 assembly: expire on silence, follow drift; VERSION
 0.7.1+rr.4

Off air 2026-11-25 (20 m, Normal): an 8-frame directed message came
out as its first two frames, the rest as loose pieces. Two rules in the
inline assembler:

- Buffers were force-completed 60 s after their FIRST frame (checked every
  15 s), so any Normal message longer than ~5 frames was cut mid-send. Now
  a buffer ends on 8 frame periods of silence, or 600 s in all.
- Buffers were keyed by qRound(freq / 10): a rig drifting across a bucket
  edge (2096.9 -> 2092.3 Hz) lost every frame past it. Now a frame joins
  the nearest open buffer within 10 Hz of its last-heard offset.

The assembly moves to src/frameassembler.h (Qt Core only) with
cpp_tests/test_frameassembler.cpp replaying the off-air frames; the test
fails against both old rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
